            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you have no running lights on your trailer, it's not something to ignore until your next stop. Running lights play a critical role in keeping your trailer visible during nighttime driving, storms, and low-visibility road conditions. When they stop working, your safety, compliance, and delivery schedule can all be affected.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators and fleet managers, electrical issues can quickly turn into costly downtime if they are not handled early. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we understand how important dependable equipment is to your business. Our team works with customers every day to diagnose electrical problems, provide quality parts, and help keep trailers road-ready. If your trailer running lights stop working, here's where to start.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-common-reasons",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Reasons You Have No Running Lights on Trailer",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "common-reasons"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Trailer lighting systems rely on several electrical components working together correctly. If one part of the system fails, your running lights may stop functioning entirely.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Some of the most common causes include:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-common-reasons-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Damaged wiring"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Corroded electrical connectors"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Faulty ground connections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Blown fuses"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Failed light assemblies"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Damaged semi trailer electrical cord"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Faulty semi trailer electrical connector"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-reasons-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical problems often develop gradually over time due to road vibration, moisture exposure, and regular wear and tear.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-connector",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Check the Semi Trailer Electrical Connector First",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "connector"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-connector-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "One of the first places to inspect is the semi trailer electrical connector. This connector links your truck's electrical system to the trailer and powers the running lights, brake lights, and turn signals.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-connector-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Over time, connectors can develop problems such as:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-connector-3",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 4
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 20
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "cards-connector-3-1",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-connector-3-1-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Corroded terminals"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Bent pins"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "cards-connector-3-2",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-connector-3-2-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Loose wiring"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Dirt buildup"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Moisture damage"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-connector-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A damaged semi trailer electrical connector can interrupt power flow and cause partial or complete lighting failure. If you notice corrosion or damaged pins, <a href=\"/service\">replacing the connector</a> may be necessary to restore proper function.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/no-running-lights-on-trailer-start-here/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician working at the service bench with a red toolbox"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-cord",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Inspect the Semi Trailer Electrical Cord",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "cord"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cord-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The semi trailer electrical cord also experiences constant stress from movement, weather, and vibration. Worn or damaged cords are a common reason for no running lights on trailer systems.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cord-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Look for signs like:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-cord-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Cracked insulation"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Frayed wires"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Loose plug connections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Pinched sections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Exposed copper wiring"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cord-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Even minor cord damage can create inconsistent lighting performance that becomes worse over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-cord-5-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-cord-5",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 26,
                          "paddingRight": 28,
