                                "style": "link"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-dont-ignore",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Don't Ignore Trailer Lighting Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "dont-ignore"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-dont-ignore-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Some drivers continue operating with trailer brake lights not working or missing running lights because the trailer still seems functional during daylight hours. The problem is that lighting failures can quickly create dangerous situations on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-dont-ignore-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Reduced Visibility Creates Safety Risks",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-dont-ignore-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Running lights help other drivers see your trailer at night, during rain, or in low-light conditions. Without them, other vehicles may misjudge your distance or fail to notice your trailer entirely. Keeping your lighting system working properly helps improve safety for everyone on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-dont-ignore-4",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "DOT Violations Can Lead to Downtime",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-dont-ignore-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Commercial trailers are required to meet federal lighting standards. If an inspection reveals no running lights on trailer systems or trailer brake lights not working, drivers may face citations or even out-of-service orders. Unexpected downtime means delayed loads, missed deadlines, and unnecessary repair expenses.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-dont-ignore-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical Issues Usually Get Worse",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-dont-ignore-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Small electrical problems rarely stay small for long. A damaged wire or loose connection can eventually affect additional systems, including brake lights, ABS systems, and trailer signals. Fixing problems early helps prevent larger repairs later.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-warning-signs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Signs Your Trailer Electrical System Needs Attention",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "warning-signs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "In some cases, running lights fail completely. In others, the system may show warning signs before total failure occurs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Watch for:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-warning-signs-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "bullet",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Flickering lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Dim trailer lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Intermittent lighting issues"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Corrosion near connectors"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Repeated blown fuses"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Moisture inside light housings"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Loose wiring connections"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you notice these issues, <a href=\"/contact\">scheduling an inspection sooner</a> rather than later can help avoid roadside problems.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/no-running-lights-on-trailer-start-here/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State service advisor speaking with a customer at the front counter"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-ready",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keep Your Trailer Ready for the Road",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "ready"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-ready-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical problems can disrupt your entire operation if they're left unresolved. At Sun State Trailers, our parts and service team helps customers diagnose lighting issues quickly and get back on the road with confidence.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventive",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive Maintenance Helps Avoid Electrical Failures",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventive"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "One of the best ways to reduce trailer lighting issues is through regular inspections and maintenance. Electrical systems should always be part of your trailer maintenance routine.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>A strong inspection checklist should include:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-preventive-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Testing running lights and brake lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Inspecting the semi trailer electrical cord"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Cleaning electrical connectors"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Checking ground connections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Inspecting light assemblies for cracks or moisture"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Verifying wiring integrity"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Routine maintenance helps identify wear before it creates major electrical failures.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-preventive-5",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When Professional Trailer Repair Makes Sense",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-6",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Some electrical issues are easy to spot, but others require advanced diagnostics to find the root cause. Modern trailer electrical systems can become complex, especially when hidden wiring damage or grounding problems are involved.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>You should <a href=\"/contact\">schedule professional repair</a> if:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-preventive-8",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Running lights fail repeatedly"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Multiple lighting systems stop working"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Wiring damage is visible"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Electrical connectors are corroded"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Fuses continue blowing"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lights work intermittently"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-schedule",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Schedule Parts and Service With Sun State Trailers",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "schedule"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-schedule-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For many trucking businesses, trailers are more than equipment. They are how drivers support their families, serve customers, and keep operations moving every day. That's why dependable trailer repair and maintenance matter. Whether you need electrical diagnostics, replacement parts, or routine service, our service department will help you get back on schedule as quickly as possible.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
